| `make test` `[local]` | Runs the whole test suite, including `slow` tests, on `tests.workers` pytest-xdist workers (`-n auto --dist worksteal`) and reports the `tests.durations` slowest durations. Work stealing lets idle workers take queued tests from a busy worker. The full gate refuses selection by `-k`, `-m`, node id or `--deselect` on the command line or in shlex-parsed `PYTEST_ADDOPTS`, and refuses malformed quoting. Every extra token must match the configured harmless flag/value allowlist. | `make test` | [`PYTHONPATH`](settings.md#make-variables), [`JUNIT_XML`](settings.md#make-variables), [`tests.workers`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`tests.durations`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | Not lint or types. `make test-ship` uses the same worker count and scheduler for its configured renderer modules. A tier target (`make unit` and the rest) and a direct `pytest` stay in one process, may narrow, and write no gate evidence. `make verify` and the gate runner strip `PYTEST_ADDOPTS` through the child-env allowlist; the full-gate flag travels on pytest's command line. | [dev-loops.md](../guides/dev-loops.md) | always |
